# {{project_title}}

> Generated with `aistrap` using the `ml-project` template.

A scikit-learn project with a complete, working example workflow: train a model,
save it, and make predictions with it. The example uses the built-in iris
dataset so everything runs right away - swap in your own data when you are ready.

## Project structure

```
{{project_name}}/
├── app/
│   ├── config.py     # Settings loaded from the environment
│   ├── train.py      # Train, evaluate and save the model
│   └── predict.py    # Load the model and predict
├── config/           # Configuration files
├── data/             # Datasets (git-ignored by default)
├── models/           # Trained model artifacts (git-ignored by default)
